# Clean Markdown Output

When creating or editing markdown files (.md), always follow these formatting rules:

- Add a blank line before and after every heading (#, ##, ###, etc.)
- Add a blank line before and after every list (bullet or numbered)
- Add a blank line before and after every code block
- Add a blank line before and after every horizontal rule (---)
- Start numbered lists at 1 (do not continue numbering from a previous section)
- Do not put trailing punctuation (colons, periods) in heading text
- Do not wrap heading text in bold (**) — the heading marker itself provides emphasis
- Use consistent table formatting with spaces around pipe characters
